-    // A current correction owns the motion until the center of the band is
-    // reached. This is what turns kiting into one continuous run instead of
-    // repeated one- or two-yard adjustments at the edge of the band.
+    // Minimum/maximum are a real comfort band, not merely entry thresholds for
+    // a correction all the way to one exact preferred point. Cross only a
+    // small edge buffer before yielding so latency does not immediately flip
